---
interface Props {
  /** 'inline' for a one-line marker, 'panel' for the full explanation. */
  variant?: 'inline' | 'panel';
}
const { variant = 'inline' } = Astro.props;

/*
  The Versa figures are the sizing ladder's design targets, not Stovehaus
  measurements. The guidelines are blunt about this — replace placeholders with
  tested specifications before anything is published or sent to a customer — so
  where we cannot yet do that, we say which kind of number a reader is looking
  at rather than letting it pass as measured.

  Steel, not ember: this is a status, not a figure, and the line colours are a
  code that stops working the moment they are spent on something else.
*/
---

{
  variant === 'inline' ? (
    <p class="spec text-steel">Provisional — design target, not yet tested</p>
  ) : (
    <div class="border border-hairline bg-surface-200 p-8">
      <p class="eyebrow text-steel">About these figures</p>
      <p class="body-copy mt-3 text-ink">
        Every figure on this page is a design target, not a measurement. It is what the stove is
        being built to, not what we have put on a meter.
      </p>
      <p class="body-copy mt-4 text-ink-muted">
        We publish a tested number once we have fired the stove and written it down. Until then
        the target is what we have, and we would rather tell you which one you are reading.
        Clearances to combustibles are not on this page at all — an installer quotes a job off
        them, and they belong to a tested appliance.
      </p>
    </div>
  )
}
